  "notes": "Alpamayo 1.5 10B (the Alpamayo-1.5-10B checkpoint, alpamayo1.5 pinned at 7a8f1c7), driven on Paddock 2eaedb5 (main after #159 and #160) over every route of bench2drive220.xml at Bench2Drive 7ec25d1, the routes set aside for every model left out (issue #158, the 220-route protocol). Its three front cameras from paddock's rig, and the route as navigation text (ALPAMAYO_NAV 1). Asked at its declared planning_hz of 10 (one /infer every 0.1 s, the last plan followed in between), the agent waiting up to 600 s for a plan (PADDOCK_INFER_TIMEOUT_S; the default is 120 s); early stop at 30 s without 3 m of progress or 4x Think2Drive's time; up to three attempts a route; no site value for anything model.yaml declares; 2 workers on each of two A100 80GB, 8 Nov 10:33 to 9 Nov 14:41 UTC. 4 route(s) set aside for every model (3800: CARLA crashes (signal 11) 63-69 s into the route on every attempt by Alpamayo 1.5 at its declared 10 Hz; 11715: CARLA crashes (signal 11) about 54 s into the route on every attempt, whichever model drives; 23695: CARLA crashes (signal 11) about 40 s into the route on every attempt by Alpamayo 1.5 at its declared 10 Hz; 24071: CARLA crashes (signal 11) 37-40 s into the route on every attempt by Alpamayo 1.5 at its declared 10 Hz): a route the simulator fails on every time measures no model, so it is in no mean and not counted as lost. 57 of 57 source runs kept no run.json, so their routes are attributed to alpamayo15 on the tree they were found in; config.model_env and the rest of config are what 57/57 source runs recorded. asked for a plan at 10 Hz, the planning_hz the model's model.yaml declared for these runs, the last plan followed in between. early stop (30 s without 3 m of route progress or 4x the expert's time on the route (none on the 9 route(s) here with no expert drive)): a car in a driving scene is expected to move, to finish in reasonable time and not to collide, so a route ended this way is a failed drive, scored as it stood when it ended (a collision's penalty included).",
